<urn:atm:triage:resolution/AY2-QA-007/1>
  a triage:Resolution ;
  triage:resolvedBy "quality-mgr" ;
  triage:resolvedAt "2026-09-06T23:45:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:fixCommit "6021aa630" ;
  triage:fixBranch "feature/ay2-herdr-transport-seam" ;
  triage:verifiedInRound "qa-pr1269-r3" ;
  triage:resolutionNote "On feature/ay2-herdr-transport-seam (arch-ctm): transport_fixture.rs is now file-level #![cfg(feature = \"test-utils\")]-gated, so bare `cargo test -p atm-herdr` compiles cleanly (13 unit tests, 0 fixture tests, no E0432) and the sprint doc's required-validation line was updated to `cargo test -p atm-herdr --all-features`. Confirmed by rust-qa-agent (direct command execution) and arch-qa (gating mechanism matches the crate's three pre-existing test-utils idioms). This closes the literal compile-failure defect this record describes. NOTE: fully gating the file behind test-utils converted the visible compile failure into a silent CI-coverage gap -- CI never enables test-utils, so the fixture suite still never runs under the merge gate. That distinct, more consequential defect is tracked as new finding AY2-QA-008 (Blocking), not as a reopening of this record." .